{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1418246-creatures-birthrights","id":1418246,"title":"Creatures Birthrights","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-14T14:27:26-07:00","id":1418246,"title":"Creatures Birthrights","content":"Hey guys!<br /> <br /> Anyone knows where i can find the rules to create Creatures?<br /> <br /> On Birthright section on Hero i only have found what Dice pool o should use , i missing something? Creatures should have HP/Defense /Secondary pools right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T16:44:29-07:00","id":1418268,"title":"","content":"This is really something that needs to be included in a future supplement, but as far as I'm aware all you can do is compare the primary pool, after any reductions from qualities or flairs, to an already available Archetype in Origin or Hero with the same number of primary pool dice, and then fill in the rest of the stats with that. In a pinch, I'd say that secondary pools are always two less than primary, desperation are always two less than secondary (Min, 2), base Health is equal to dot level, and base Defense is 1 less than Health (Min. 1). Then make any adjustments due to qualities after that, such as increased Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T06:34:16-07:00","id":1418354,"title":"","content":"Here's what I use. Creatures have an amount of Health equal to their Rank (or the Health of the creature they are based on) and a Defense equal to their Rank divided by 2 (rounded up). Their Secondary and Desperation dice pools depend on their remaining Primary dice after purchasing Qualities, Flairs and Flaws. Consult the following table:<br /> <br /> Primary, Secondary, Desperation<br /> 3, 2, 1<br /> 4, 3, 1<br /> 5, 4, 2<br /> 6, 4, 2<br /> 7, 5, 3<br /> 8, 6, 4<br /> 9, 7, 4<br /> 10, 8, 5<br /> 11, 9, 5<br /> 12, 10, 5<br /> 13, 11, 6<br /> 14, 12, 6<br /> 15, 13, 7","signature":"","edited":{"userid":972,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","user":"Fairlyhyperman","date":".  Sorry, table formatting does not appear to be sticking. 10-15-2020, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","name":"Fairlyhyperman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T10:01:34-07:00","id":1418387,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers guys, i Will try work with you guys ideas and see whats work best with my group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5311-thiagocord","name":"Thiagocord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T10:28:22-07:00","id":1418391,"title":"","content":"The way I interpreted the Creature Birthright is that they have a very broad dice and ability pool for general use. The drawback is that they have no health pool or defense and gain the Taken Out condition whenever they are attacked. <br /> <br /> In my game, the creature is loyal but practical to a fault and will not help if it will get hurt in the process (since its a noble griffin who is much too important to deal with the poors when it doesn't suit his needs).<br /> <br /> I see Followers as more specialized Creatures that, in exchange, are able to take hits and actively help during an action scene.<br /> <br /> If you want to, you can just add stats to a Creature by giving it the Super Soldier or Martial Artist Quality (pg 146 of Origin) for free. I'd still keep the broad dice pool though to differentiate creatures from Followers, keeping in mind it's still an animal and can only help in specific ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25184-chaoticsilly","name":"chaoticsilly","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T11:06:30-07:00","id":1418394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>chaoticsilly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1418246-creatures-birthrights?p=1418391#post1418391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I interpreted the Creature Birthright is that they have a very broad dice and ability pool for general use. The drawback is that they have no health pool or defense and gain the Taken Out condition whenever they are attacked.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Creatures <i>do</i> have Health. There's a sidebar in Hero that says they have Health equal to their Rank. Like, page 202 of Hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T12:40:42-07:00","id":1418403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1418246-creatures-birthrights?p=1418394#post1418394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Creatures <i>do</i> have Health. There's a sidebar in Hero that says they have Health equal to their Rank. Like, page 202 of Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I need to give my player her griffin back!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25184-chaoticsilly","name":"chaoticsilly","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"